    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n81229" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περιδεής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δέος</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>very timid</i> or <i>fearful</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. γενέσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					5.44
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				And.
				4.40
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				3.28
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Isoc.
				2.23
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Alciphr.
				2.4
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινι</span>
			<i>at</i> a thing, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				7.15
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινος</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Ep.</u>
				348b
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π.μὴ</span> . . <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				3.80
			</span></i>. Adv.-<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εῶς</span>
			<i>in great fear</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				6.83
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρός τιϝα π. σχεῖν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Isoc.
					9.58
				</span></i>
			.</div>
